// wdoc section: Charts.
page wdoc_charts { sites = [:reference]
  h1 "Charts" {}

  p "wdoc ships three chart kinds — `bar_chart`, `line_chart`, and `pie_chart` — that lower to SVG via pure-WCL geometry. Data is supplied as variant-tagged series; styling rides the same `class` and `theme` system as everything else." {}

  h2 "Bar and line charts" {}

  p "Both accept a `series: list<ChartSeries>` of `ChartSeries::Of { name, values }`. Multiple series produce grouped bars or multi-line plots." {}
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
bar_chart {
  title      = "Quarterly revenue"
  x_label    = "Quarter"
  y_label    = "USD (m)"
  categories = ["Q1", "Q2", "Q3", "Q4"]
  series     = [
    ChartSeries::Of { name: "2025", values: [12.0, 15.0, 17.0, 22.0] },
    ChartSeries::Of { name: "2026", values: [14.0, 18.0, 21.0, 25.0] },
  ]
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Pie chart" {}

  p "A `pie_chart` takes `slices: list<ChartSlice>` of `ChartSlice::Of { label, value }`. Slices are drawn as polygon-approximated arcs." {}
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
pie_chart {
  title  = "Market share"
  slices = [
    ChartSlice::Of { label: "Alpha", value: 42.0 },
    ChartSlice::Of { label: "Beta",  value: 31.0 },
    ChartSlice::Of { label: "Other", value: 27.0 },
  ]
}
WCL
  }

  h2 "Line chart annotations" {}

  p "On a `line_chart`, set `point_labels = true` to print every data point's value above its marker. For author-named annotations, pass `points: list<ChartPoint>` of `ChartPoint::At { label, category, value }` to pin a custom marker + label to a chosen `(x, y)`." {}

  h2 "Theming" {}

  p "Every bar, line, or slice is auto-tagged with a cycling palette class (`wdoc-series-1` through `wdoc-series-8`) and emits no inline fill — colour comes from CSS. Override one series by redeclaring its palette class (the name has hyphens, so quote it):" {}
  code wcl {
    source = <<'WCL'
class "wdoc-series-1" {
  fill = "#88c0d0"
  dark  { fill = "#88c0d0" }
  light { fill = "#5e81ac" }
}
WCL
  }

  callout "Built-in chart styling" {
    class = ["info"]
    body  = "wdoc injects a default chart stylesheet before user class rules, and themes set the eight series colours through --wdoc-* custom properties. So selecting a theme automatically recolours every chart."
  }

  p "Next: [Terminals & TUI](wdoc_terminals)." {}
}
